        "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
        "body": "Just to double check my understanding, `isBetter` is a (total?) ordering on type `S` (the type parameter passed to the `Scorable` typeclass), and since `badness : S -> [0, 1]`, the monotonicity statement of `isBetter a b \u2192 badness a \u2264 badness b` actually relates two orderings on different types, namely the `isBetter` relation on `S` and the \u2264 relation on `[0, 1]`. Let me know if I'm mistaken!",
